 "hypothesis": "Every installed archive ships development-only runtime tests/lockfile and repository design/audit docs (~1.06 MB) that the production kernel and user-facing docs never consume.",
 "approach": "Curate dev-only docs and runtime test/lock entries in both Python payload producers; retain three required user docs. Fix dirty-worktree skill cache leak in assemble_artifacts.py; package_release.py already filters caches. verify_release.py now rejects escaped caches; negative tests cover both producers and poisoned tar. No Rust production changes.",
 "parity_notes": "Kevin install-payload ruling verbatim: \"OPERATOR RULING (Kevin, ~01:00Z 2026-09-26) on install-payload parity for the perf hillclimb: development artifacts \u2014 dev/design docs (porting notes, parity checklists, design docs, audits), packaged dev test suites, dev lockfiles \u2014 are EXEMPT from the install-payload parity contract and may be cut from shipped installs. User-facing docs (RUST_QUICKSTART.md, keybindings.md, MODEL-SURFACE.md) are NOT exempt and must ship. Product behavior, runtime, skills, and the binary are unchanged by this ruling. Adversarial reviewers: treat this as a standing contract amendment; a lane cutting dev artifacts with user docs kept is NOT a capability BLOCK, but must document the removed-file list, per-category bytes, and quote this ruling in the record + PR body. Context: perf-install-tree lane removed 1.06MB non-binary (54.4% dev docs / 32.4% dev tests / 13.2% uv.lock) with byte-identical binaries.\" Corrected PR 966d93292 retains MODEL-SURFACE.md, RUST_QUICKSTART.md, keybindings.md, AND FEATURE_PARITY.md because quickstart links locally to that feature-status doc. Both packers fail closed on each of four missing docs; relative file targets resolve in both installed tarballs (24/24 release tests). Same-VM current-base binary SHA/size measured below; 91eed/bc1 old docs claim superseded. Skills/catalog unchanged after filtering ignored generated bytecode. Decoder/runtime behavior separate and unchanged by packaging-only diff.",
